III. ALTERNATIVES
General 
At present, within the Milwaukee Metropolitan Area, vehicular traffic desiring access to General Mitchell Field is able to use a portion of the Interstate System but then must exit at various interchanges located two to three miles from the airport and travel the remaining distance on the existing local arterial street system to reach the airport. All access to and from the airport from the freeway involves travel over Howell Avenue, in combination with either Layton Avenue, South 27th Street, Howard Avenue or College Avenue. Since completion of Interstate Routes I-94 and I-894 in November of 1966, these streets have been serving through traffic and airport oriented traffic, as well as providing local property access.
We recommend constructing the Airport Spur, freeway facility, on new location, within Corridor No. 5, to provide for improved ground access to General Mitchell Field by linking the airport entrance road to the nearest Interstate Route. Other courses of action, however, are available that would improve access to General Mitchell Field and are discussed as follows:
Alternative Courses of Action
Alternative proposals that have been considered in the planning stages as alternates to implementation of the proposed project are:
1. Upgrading Grange Avenue from Howell Avenue to I-94 into a multi-lane highway;
2. "Do Nothing" alternate;
3. Improvement of local streets and arterial highways, "no build";
4. Rapid transit service;
5. Alternative freeway corridor locations.
